    {
      "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019-sch-1-sec-6on",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6ON Protection of certain information given to the Child Sexual",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019#sch-1-sec-6on"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "Abuse Royal Commission\n\n(1) This section applies to information if:\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nRoyal Commissions Amendment (Private Sessions) Act 2019\nNo. 64, 2019\n\n(a) the information was given by, or on behalf of, a natural\nperson to the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission other\nthan for the purposes of a private session; and\n\n(b) the information contains an account of:\n\n(i) the natural person’s experiences of child sexual abuse in\nan institutional context; or\n\n(ii) what happened to other people regarding child sexual\nabuse in an institutional context; and\n\n(c) the information identifies the natural person who gave the\ninformation, or on whose behalf the information was given;\nand\n\n(d) the Commission indicated that the information, if given,\nwould be treated as confidential; and\n\n(e) the information was treated as confidential by the\nCommission.\n\n(2) Section 6OE applies in relation to the information as if it were a\nstatement or disclosure made by the natural person at a private\nsession for the Commission.\n\n(3) Sections 6OH, 6OK and 6OL apply in relation to the information\nas if it were information given by the natural person at a private\nsession for the Commission.\n\n(4) Section 6OM applies in relation to the information as if it were a\nrecord that contains information obtained at a private session for\nthe Commission.",
      "skos:definition": "Abuse Royal Commission\n\n(1) This section applies to information if:\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nRoyal Commissions Amendment (Private Sessions) Act 2019\nNo. 64, 2019\n\n(a) the information was given by, or on behalf of, a natural\nperson to the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission other\nthan for the purposes of a private session; and\n\n(b) the information contains an account of:\n\n(i) the natural person’s experiences of child sexual abuse in\nan institutional context; or\n\n(ii) what happened to other people regarding child sexual\nabuse in an institutional context; and\n\n(c) the information identifies the natural person who gave the\ninformation, or on whose behalf the information was given;\nand\n\n(d) the Commission indicated that the information, if given,\nwould be treated as confidential; and\n\n(e) the information was treated as confidential by the\nCommission.\n\n(2) Section 6OE applies in relation to the information as if it were a\nstatement or disclosure made by the natural person at a private\nsession for the Commission.\n\n(3) Sections 6OH, 6OK and 6OL apply in relation to the information\nas if it were information given by the natural person at a private\nsession for the Commission.\n\n(4) Section 6OM applies in relation to the information as if it were a\nrecord that contains information obtained at a private session for\nthe Commission.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019-sch-1-sec-6on-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019-sch-1-sec-6on-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019-sch-1-sec-6on-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019-sch-1-sec-6on-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "53114290c70bea45a45ee1bfa67e0a15af3f73cfb0893fcaaf5fe4039a1a49db"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019#sch-1-sec-6on",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6ON Protection of certain information given to the Child Sexual",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "Abuse Royal Commission\n\n(1) This section applies to information if:\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nRoyal Commissions Amendment (Private Sessions) Act 2019\nNo. 64, 2019\n\n(a) the information was given by, or on behalf of, a natural\nperson to the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission other\nthan for the purposes of a private session; and\n\n(b) the information contains an account of:\n\n(i) the natural person’s experiences of child sexual abuse in\nan institutional context; or\n\n(ii) what happened to other people regarding child sexual\nabuse in an institutional context; and\n\n(c) the information identifies the natural person who gave the\ninformation, or on whose behalf the information was given;\nand\n\n(d) the Commission indicated that the information, if given,\nwould be treated as confidential; and\n\n(e) the information was treated as confidential by the\nCommission.\n\n(2) Section 6OE applies in relation to the information as if it were a\nstatement or disclosure made by the natural person at a private\nsession for the Commission.\n\n(3) Sections 6OH, 6OK and 6OL apply in relation to the information\nas if it were information given by the natural person at a private\nsession for the Commission.\n\n(4) Section 6OM applies in relation to the information as if it were a\nrecord that contains information obtained at a private session for\nthe Commission."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019-sch-1-sec-6on-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6ON(1) Protection of certain information given to the Child Sexual",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019#sch-1-sec-6on-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to information if:\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nRoyal Commissions Amendment (Private Sessions) Act 2019\nNo. 64, 2019\n\n(a) the information was given by, or on behalf of, a natural\nperson to the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission other\nthan for the purposes of a private session; and\n\n(b) the information contains an account of:\n\n(i) the natural person’s experiences of child sexual abuse in\nan institutional context; or\n\n(ii) what happened to other people regarding child sexual\nabuse in an institutional context; and\n\n(c) the information identifies the natural person who gave the\ninformation, or on whose behalf the information was given;\nand\n\n(d) the Commission indicated that the information, if given,\nwould be treated as confidential; and\n\n(e) the information was treated as confidential by the\nCommission.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to information if:\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nRoyal Commissions Amendment (Private Sessions) Act 2019\nNo. 64, 2019\n\n(a) the information was given by, or on behalf of, a natural\nperson to the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission other\nthan for the purposes of a private session; and\n\n(b) the information contains an account of:\n\n(i) the natural person’s experiences of child sexual abuse in\nan institutional context; or\n\n(ii) what happened to other people regarding child sexual\nabuse in an institutional context; and\n\n(c) the information identifies the natural person who gave the\ninformation, or on whose behalf the information was given;\nand\n\n(d) the Commission indicated that the information, if given,\nwould be treated as confidential; and\n\n(e) the information was treated as confidential by the\nCommission.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-private-sessions-act-2019-sch-1-sec-6on"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
